        "point": "access pattern",
        "statement": "The translation by a concrete real number x is obtained as VTask.translate (Multiplicative.ofAdd x); the Multiplicative.ofAdd wrapper is always required to pass a real number into the domain.",
        "note": "standard additive-to-multiplicative bridge in Mathlib"
      },
      {
        "point": "identity",
        "statement": "VTask.translate maps the multiplicative identity (Multiplicative.ofAdd 0) to the identity unit in CircleDeg1Liftˣ, whose underlying function is the identity on ℝ.",
        "note": "follows from map_one of the monoid hom"
      },
      {
        "point": "inverse",
        "statement": "The inverse of VTask.translate (Multiplicative.ofAdd x) in CircleDeg1Liftˣ is VTask.translate (Multiplicative.ofAdd (-x)), i.e., translation by the negation.",
        "note": "group-inverse corresponds to additive negation under ofAdd"
      }
    ]
  },
